Z||000000||FieroPerformance||08-08-2001||01:24 PM||||Do not buy from American Auto Accessories (3A racing). I bought a set of $60 fog lights thinking that I was getting reasonable quality for the high price. Within 2 weeks a bulb burnt out and both lenses were cracked. I opened it up to see if I could replace the bulb and noticed that the fancy chrome finish on the inside was now just rust. I sent several emails to the company about getting a replacement with no response. So about 3 months ago I sent them to 3A racing's address. I just called them today and couldn't even understand what the people that work there were saying because non of them speak english very well at all.<BR>     Normally I would consider these a lemon and wouldn't condem the company, but a friend of mine had the same thing happen to him.<P>O yeah, here is a picture of what these fine quality products looked like after being on my car for about 3 weeks:<P>  <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/foglight.jpg">  <P>-Charlie<BR> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroPerformance (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||08-08-2001||02:26 PM||||Thanks for the tip.<P>Junk merchants NEED to be out of business.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000002||Reality||08-08-2001||10:41 PM||||I know I'm going to regret this in the end but here goes. I hope you didn't pay bunches for those lights to begin with, cause you could of went to Kmart and bought them and not have paid shipping. Don't get me wrong I'm not putting Kmart down, mainly cause thast my employer. But hey thought I would let you know. I just mention it, cause I was looking at the exact same set of lights yesterday. ||||reg||9
